Z||000000||LAMBO||11-21-2000||02:00 PM||||I've had my new little 84 se for about two weeks now and just the other day, the throw out bearing starts to make a terrible racket. I'm going to take the long weekend to tear in and replace it. Anybody have any tips or suggestions for making this as painless as possible? I plan to keep the cradle bolted up and just pull the tranny from the motor while supporting the motor with a hoist. I will be replacing axel seals as well. Anything  else I should replace while its apart?<BR>Todd||||reg||9
Z||000001||StuGood||11-21-2000||05:11 PM||||Not speaking from experience, but think I would go ahead and replace the disc and pressure plate, if I went to the trouble of pulling the Xaxle.  Unless they're practically brand new, or if you aren't planning to keep the car.<P>BTW, on V6's, the cam end plate should be resealed at the same time; not sure what's there for 4's. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||11-21-2000||07:47 PM||||DEfinatly what stu said.... replace the whole clutch. doing the bearing only on these cars isn't saving anything.||||reg||1
